<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A text input that suggests matching options as you type.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/autocomplete)

<%= embed UI::AutocompletePreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Autocomplete(items: frameworks) do
  AutocompleteInput(placeholder: "Search a framework")
  AutocompleteContent do
    AutocompleteEmpty { "No frameworks found." }
    AutocompleteList do |item|
      AutocompleteItem(value: item) { item }
    end
  end
end
```

Autocomplete is a compound component. The root holds the data (`items:`) and shared options
(`size:`, `variant:`, `clearable:`, `icon:`); the parts compose the input and the filtered popup:

- **AutocompleteInput** - the text field, styled like Input. Add a clear button with `clearable:`
  and a dropdown chevron with `icon:` (both on the root, both off by default).
- **AutocompleteContent** - the popup. It opens below the input and flips above it when there
  isn't room.
- **AutocompleteList** - the scrollable list. Pass a block with an argument to map over the
  filtered items, or static `AutocompleteItem`s.
- **AutocompleteItem** - one option; its `value:` is what selection writes into the input.
- **AutocompleteEmpty** - shown only when the filter matches nothing.

Filtering, keyboard navigation and the ARIA combobox state come from the `ui--autocomplete`
Stimulus controller.

## Examples

### Variants

`variant:` switches the input between a bordered outline (default) and a filled soft field.

<%= embed UI::AutocompletePreview, :variants %>

```ruby
Autocomplete(items: frameworks, variant: :soft) do
  AutocompleteInput(placeholder: "Search a framework")
  # ...
end
```

### Sizes

`size:` on the root scales the input, popup radius, and items together.

<%= embed UI::AutocompletePreview, :sizes %>

```ruby
Autocomplete(items: frameworks, size: :lg) { ... }
```

### Clearable & chevron

`clearable:` adds a clear (✕) button once there's a value, `icon:` a chevron that toggles the
popup. Both render inside the input.

<%= embed UI::AutocompletePreview, :clearable %>

```ruby
Autocomplete(items: frameworks, default_value: "Next.js", clearable: true, icon: true) { ... }
```

### Items with icons

Items can render any content. Mark a leading icon with `data: { icon: "start" }` so it gets the
same inner spacing as in Button. When items are objects rather than strings, give the root an
`item_to_string_value:` (a key, method name or proc) so the filter and input know how to read
each one. `start_slot: :selected_icon` mirrors the selected item's icon into the input.

<%= embed UI::AutocompletePreview, :object_items %>

```ruby
Autocomplete(items: commands, item_to_string_value: :label, clearable: true, icon: true) do
  AutocompleteInput(placeholder: "Search commands", start_slot: :selected_icon)
  AutocompleteContent do
    AutocompleteEmpty { "No commands found." }
    AutocompleteList do |command|
      AutocompleteItem(value: command) do
        svg(data: { icon: "start" }, ...) { |s| s.path(d: command[:icon]) }
        plain command[:label]
      end
    end
  end
end
```

### Grouped options

Pass grouped items (`{ value:, items: }`) and render each group with `AutocompleteGroup` +
`AutocompleteLabel` + `AutocompleteCollection`. The outer block iterates groups;
`AutocompleteCollection` renders the items inside each.

<%= embed UI::AutocompletePreview, :grouped %>

```ruby
Autocomplete(items: produce) do
  AutocompleteInput(placeholder: "Search produce")
  AutocompleteContent do
    AutocompleteEmpty { "No produce found." }
    AutocompleteList do |group|
      AutocompleteGroup(items: group[:items]) do
        AutocompleteLabel { group[:value] }
        AutocompleteCollection { |item| AutocompleteItem(value: item) { item } }
      end
    end
  end
end
```

### Grid layout

`grid: true` lays options out in a grid (arrow keys move in two dimensions).
`AutocompleteList(cols:)` controls how many items per row.

<%= embed UI::AutocompletePreview, :grid %>

```ruby
Autocomplete(items: libraries, grid: true, icon: true) do
  AutocompleteInput(placeholder: "Search a library")
  AutocompleteContent do
    AutocompleteList(cols: 2) { |item| AutocompleteItem(value: item, class: "flex-1") { item } }
  end
end
```

### Static items & forms

Static `AutocompleteItem` children work too. `name:` submits the typed or selected value with
the surrounding form; `disabled: true` on an item skips it in navigation.

<%= embed UI::AutocompletePreview, :static_items %>

### Listening for changes

The controller dispatches `ui--autocomplete:change` with `{ value }` whenever the value changes
(typing, selection, clear) - the counterpart of React's `onValueChange`. The input also fires a
native `change` event on selection.

```ruby
Autocomplete(items: frameworks, data: { action: "ui--autocomplete:change->search#update" }) { ... }
```

### RTL

The component uses logical properties, so it mirrors under `dir="rtl"`; arrow keys follow the
direction in grid mode.

<%= embed UI::AutocompletePreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

### Autocomplete

The root. Holds the data and the shared options and renders the Stimulus wrapper.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `items:` | `Array` | `[]` | The data to filter. A flat array, or `{ value:, items: }` hashes for grouped options. |
| `size:` | `:sm`, `:md`, `:lg` | `:md` | Input height, popup radius, and item sizing. |
| `variant:` | `:outline`, `:soft` | `:outline` | Input appearance - bordered or filled. |
| `clearable:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Render a clear button inside the input when a value is present. |
| `icon:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Render a chevron button that toggles the popup. |
| `grid:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Lay options out as a navigable grid instead of a list. |
| `value:` / `default_value:` | `String` | - | Initial input value. |
| `name:` | `String` | - | Input name for form submission. |
| `disabled:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Disable the input and its buttons. |
| `item_to_string_value:` | `Symbol`, `String`, `Proc` | `to_s` | How the filter and input read object items. |
| `id:`, `class:`, `data:`, … | | | Any other HTML attributes go on the root element. |

### AutocompleteInput

The text field, rendered inside an input group.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `placeholder:` | `String` | `" "` | Placeholder text. |
| `start_slot:` | `String`, `Proc`, `:selected_icon` | - | Adornment before the field. `:selected_icon` mirrors the selected item's `data-icon="start"` element. |
| `end_slot:` | `String`, `Proc` | - | Adornment after the field. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes on the input group, merged via tailwind_merge. |

Any other attributes (`aria_label:`, `required:`, `data:`, …) go on the `<input>`.

### AutocompleteContent

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `side:` | `:bottom`, `:top` | `:bottom` | Preferred side; flips when there isn't room. |
| `side_offset:` | `Integer` | `6` | Gap between the input and the popup, in px. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes on the popup. |

### AutocompleteList

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `cols:` | `Integer` | - | Items per row in grid mode. |
| block | `{ \|item\| … }` or `{ … }` | - | With an argument it's called for each item; without one it renders static children. |

### AutocompleteItem

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `value:` | `String` or item | - | The value written to the input; objects are read with `item_to_string_value`. |
| `disabled:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Skip the item in navigation and selection. |

### AutocompleteEmpty, AutocompleteGroup, AutocompleteLabel, AutocompleteCollection

`AutocompleteEmpty` is a live region shown only when nothing matches. `AutocompleteGroup(items:)`
wraps a labelled group, `AutocompleteLabel` is its heading (wired to `aria-labelledby`) and
`AutocompleteCollection { |item| … }` maps over the group's items. All accept `class:` and other
HTML attributes.

## Accessibility

- The input has `role="combobox"` with `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls` and `aria-activedescendant`
  pointing at the highlighted `role="option"`.
- Arrow keys move the highlight (both axes in grid mode), Home/End jump to the ends, Enter
  selects, Escape closes, and focus wraps back to the input past the last option.
- `AutocompleteEmpty` is a polite live region, so "no results" is announced.
- Give the input a label: `aria_label:` or a `<label for>` pointing at the input.
